---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
  - undying-tide-presentation
  - undying-tide-creatures
requires:
  - regeneration
  - creature-figures
description: Effects - every event of a run is seen as it happens, and the pages drift.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: renders the moving 3D background of :TitleScreen:, :RegenerationScreen: and the scoreboard page on a Three.js canvas behind the page content, timed by `requestAnimationFrame`, apart from the game loop.
  - Every backdrop canvas of a page lies in a layer beneath all of that page's content: the canvas has a negative `z-index`, or the content is positioned with a `z-index` above the canvas's, so no backdrop canvas paints over any heading, text, button or legend of the page.

***functional specs***

# pickup-burst
Collecting a :GeneFragment: or using up a :PlanktonCloud: shows a burst where it lay.
- A :GeneFragment: throws out 8 sparks of radius 2 px in the palette's gene-fragment colour, evenly spread, flying 30 px out and fading over 0.4 s.
- A :PlanktonCloud: throws out 10 specks of radius 1.5 px in the palette's plankton colour, evenly spread, flying 40 px out and fading over 0.5 s.

# heart-loss-effect
Losing one of the :Hearts: shows the loss: the heart going from :Hud: grows to 150% and fades out over 0.5 s where it stood, and a ring in the palette's heart colour widens from 24 px to 48 px around the :Jellyfish: and fades out over 0.3 s.
- The :Invulnerability: blink is unchanged.

# predator-dissolve
A purified :Predator: dissolves: its figure stays drawn where it was purified, growing to 130% of its size and fading out over 0.5 s, while 6 specks in the palette's sting colour rise 20 px from it and fade.
- A purified :StingingJelly: dissolves with its tentacle segments, each growing to 130% about its own centre and fading out with the bell.
- Each anchovy of a purified :AnchovySchool: dissolves where it was.
- A dissolving figure cannot touch the :Jellyfish: and is not in :StateSnapshot:.
- A :SplitJelly: that splits does not dissolve.

# level-dive-transition
Each :Level: after the first is dived into: for 0.8 s from its start it is drawn shifted 120 px down, rising to its place, under the palette's darkness overlay fading from fully opaque to clear.
- :Hud: is drawn above it, unshifted.
- The :Level: plays as usual during the 0.8 s.

# drifting-screen-background
:TitleScreen: and :RegenerationScreen: have a drifting 3D background: 12 3D mote spheres of radius 2 to 5 px in the palette's bell colour at 25% opacity rise at 15 to 30 px/s, swaying up to 10 px to either side of their line, and come back in at the bottom after leaving at the top.
- :TitleScreen: draws them over the sunlit water gradient of the palette.
- :RegenerationScreen: draws them over the :Level: as it stood at the :RunEnd:.
- Their sizes, speeds and starting places are the same every time the screen opens.
- Every heading, text line, button and legend of :TitleScreen:, :RegenerationScreen: and the scoreboard page is drawn above the background and stays visible.

# polyp-transformation-effect
The :Jellyfish: shrinks into its 3D :Polyp: (`public/models/anemone.glb` attached via `attachGlbModel` in `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` with `userData.glbModel = "anemone.glb"` over its sculpted 3D fallback figure) and unfurls out of it: over the first 0.4 s of the :Polyp: stage, the 3D :Jellyfish: figure, tentacles with it, shrinks to 40% and fades out while the 3D polyp figure grows from 40% to its full size and fades in; over the last 0.4 s the same is played backwards.
- Both 3D figures scale about the :Jellyfish: centre.
- Between the two, only the 3D polyp figure is drawn, at its full size but for its pulse.
- The :Jellyfish: does not pulse while it is a :Polyp:.
- The polyp figure pulses while a :Polyp:, from the end of its growing until its shrinking starts: the polyp figure swells to 112% of its full size and back once every 0.8 s, timed from when its growing ended, about the :Jellyfish: centre, inside an unscaled 3D halo sphere of radius 36 in the palette's player core colour whose opacity rises from 15% to 45% and falls back on the same cycle.
- The :Polyp: circle stays radius 24 throughout.
- The polyp figure has no sharp corners: its stalk is a rounded column, its crown and foot are smooth rounded forms tinted in the palette's player colours, and every contour of the figure is smooth.
